        "original_id": "63a5b4e5-1d5c-54ae-a79a-39bbce7659f7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eli Manning, Peyton Manning, Archie Manning, David Tyree, Philip Rivers\n- Organizations: New York Giants, San Diego Chargers, National Football League\n- Places: Manning Field at John L. Guidry Stadium\n- Events: 2004 NFL Draft, Super Bowl XLII, Manning Passing Academy football camp\n- Roles: quarterback, wide receiver\n\nFacts:\n- Eli Manning was born on January 3, 1981, and is an American football quarterback for the New York Giants of the National Football League.\n- In the 2004 NFL Draft, the San Diego Chargers selected Eli Manning with the first overall pick and immediately traded him to the New York Giants in a deal highlighted by the fourth overall selection, Philip Rivers.\n- On February 3, 2008, the Helmet Catch was an American football play in the final two minutes of Super Bowl XLII involving New York Giants quarterback Eli Manning and wide receiver David Tyree.\n- Manning Field at John L. Guidry Stadium is named after the Manning family because Peyton Manning, Eli Manning, and Archie Manning hold the Manning Passing Academy football camp at the facility.",
